                  <provenance type="#b" source="2581"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_198">Eton, Buckinghamshire.
                        Royal College of the Assumption of Saint Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>In a
                        binding by Andrew Lisley, who was employed at the college in 1521.</p><p>The
                        manuscript forms a set with Eton MSS 14 and 19. They carry contents-lists
                        produced for William Horman (d. 1535), fellow of Eton. Each book has
                        suffered from damp at beginning and end, which perhaps explains why tertio
                        folio readings were chosen for the inventory (SC229.110).</p></provenance>
